corner. ]
;B[fo]CR[fo]C[Very good.

White makes a large moyo with only a few stones ( 
this means the moyo is not strong at all). In this kind of 
game, white should try to keep black weak. 
If black has a strong position, the white 'moyo' will not 
be moyo anymore but weakness. ]
;W[jd]CR[jd]C[I think it is better for white to defend on the left side, 
because the black's position on the lower left is 
stronger than the upper right.]
;B[di]CR[di]C[Because black is very strong in the lower left corner, 
black can invade easily.]
;W[el]CR[el];B[cf]CR[cf]C[The fuseki looks good for black, because the black 
stones are more efficient than white's. ]
;W[ef]CR[ef]
(;B[dc]CR[dc]C[A nice move, but not good for this situation. And it 
is not necessary at all for black to play like this.
There is a important idea in the game of Go, that is\: 
our opponent may have something. It is very 
dangerous to take away everything from him, in that 
case we just put ourself in danger. 
See variation.]
